  "motionSource": { "description": "Where the motion values that are not plain numbers come from, so a test recomputes them rather than trusting them. spring is the sibling app's (Chela's) arrival spring in SwiftUI's own terms, the defaults of .spring(); CSS has no spring, so core/kit/rules/motion.js springCurve() samples it into the linear() easing and the duration motion.spring-ease and motion.spring carry. screen, spring and min-visible are Chela's tokens of the same name (its core/spec/tokens.json motion block): screen is how long a screen inside a surface takes to move, on the sheet's curve; spring is how a first screen arrives (the onboarding form here, the pairing screen there); min-visible is the floor on how long a transient state stays on screen before it may be replaced.", "spring": { "response-ms": 550, "damping-fraction": 0.825 } },
